---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const title = "Terms of Service — NexQL";
const description =
  "Terms of Service for NexQL, the PostgreSQL VS Code extension and its optional paid Sponsor/Singularity plans.";
const canonical = "https://nexql.astrx.dev/terms";
---

<LegalLayout {title} {description} {canonical} active="terms">
  <main class="legal-main" id="legal-content">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="grad-text legal-h1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: July 19, 2026</p>
    <p class="legal-intro">
      NexQL is a free, MIT-licensed PostgreSQL extension for VS Code, with optional paid
      <strong>Sponsor</strong> and <strong>Singularity</strong> plans. These Terms cover the
      <a href="https://nexql.astrx.dev/">nexql.astrx.dev</a> website, the paid checkout/licensing
      backend, and the optional Cloud Sync and hosted AI features. They're written to be short and
      readable — if anything is unclear, email
      <a href="mailto:support@astrx.dev">support@astrx.dev</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="legal-prose">
      <h2>1. Who runs NexQL</h2>
      <p>
        NexQL is developed and operated by <strong>astrx.dev</strong> (GitHub:
        <a href="https://github.com/dev-asterix" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >dev-asterix</a
        >). In these Terms, "we", "us", and "NexQL" refer to astrx.dev acting as the operator of this
        website and backend services. We're an independent developer project, not a large company —
        if you ever need a human, email works.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The extension is free and open source</h2>
      <p>
        The core NexQL extension (
        <a
          href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ric-v.postgres-explorer"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">VS Code Marketplace</a
        >
        /
        <a
          href="https://open-vsx.org/extension/ric-v/postgres-explorer"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Open VSX</a
        >) is MIT-licensed and free forever — notebooks, database explorer, AI assist (including
        zero-config NexQL Free AI), schema tools, and safety controls. Source is public at
        <a href="https://github.com/dev-asterix/NexQL" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >github.com/dev-asterix/NexQL</a
        >
        under the MIT license, which governs your right to use, modify, and redistribute the code
        independently of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Paid plans (Sponsor / Singularity)</h2>
      <p>
        Sponsor and Singularity are optional paid subscriptions that unlock extra features (schema
        diff, unlimited saved queries, cloud sync, higher AI usage limits, priority support). They
        are billed monthly or annually, in INR or USD, and renew automatically until cancelled.
        Current pricing is shown on the <a href="/#pricing">pricing page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Payments</h2>
      <p>
        All payments are processed by
        <a href="https://razorpay.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Razorpay</a>, a
        licensed payment aggregator that supports Indian and international cards/currencies. We never
        see or store your full card number — Razorpay handles that per their own
        <a href="https://razorpay.com/security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >security and compliance</a
        >
        standards (PCI-DSS). After a successful payment, we receive a license key that activates your
        plan in VS Code.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cancellations &amp; refunds</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel anytime from the license management screen (or by emailing us your license
        key). Cancelling stops future renewals; by default your plan stays active until the end of
        the billing period you already paid for. You may also request an immediate cancellation,
        which ends access right away.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>We do not offer refunds</strong> for partial billing periods, unused time, or
        change-of-mind cancellations. If you believe you were charged in error (e.g. a duplicate
        charge or a billing bug), email <a href="mailto:support@astrx.dev">support@astrx.dev</a> with
        your license key and we'll look into it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Don't attempt to bypass, share, or resell license keys or the free-tier usage limits.</li>
        <li>Don't use the hosted AI gateway or Cloud Sync to store or transmit unlawful content.</li>
        <li>Don't attempt to overwhelm, scan, or attack the API backend.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may suspend access for accounts that violate these terms or abuse shared infrastructure.</p>

      <h2>7. AI features</h2>
      <p>
        NexQL Free AI (zero-config) and the "bring your own key" providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini,
        GitHub Models, VS Code Language Model API) generate SQL, explanations, and optimizations from
        the prompts and schema context you send. When you use your own API key, that provider's own
        terms and privacy policy govern how they handle your data — NexQL is just the client. See our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for what NexQL itself stores about AI usage (short
        version: usage counts for metering, not your prompt content).
      </p>

      <h2>8. Cloud Sync (paid feature)</h2>
      <p>
        Cloud Sync is opt-in and lets Sponsor/Singularity users sync connection profiles, saved
        queries, and notebooks across devices. Database <strong>passwords are never included</strong>
        — credentials stay local via VS Code's encrypted Secret Storage. If your paid plan lapses,
        synced data is retained for 30 days and then purged; see the Privacy Policy for details.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Database safety — use your own judgment</h2>
      <p>
        NexQL includes safety features (environment labels, risk scoring for destructive statements)
        as a convenience, not a guarantee. <strong
          >You are responsible for the SQL you run</strong
        > against your databases, including anything generated or suggested by AI. Always review
        generated queries before running them against production data.
      </p>

      <h2>10. No warranty, limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        NexQL is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. To the maximum
        extent permitted by law, astrx.dev is not liable for any indirect, incidental, or
        consequential damages — including data loss — arising from your use of the extension,
        website, or backend services.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms as the product changes. Material changes will update the "Last
        updated" date above; continued use after a change means you accept the update.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of India, where our payment processor Razorpay is
        licensed and regulated. We welcome customers worldwide — Razorpay supports international cards
        and both INR and USD billing.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms: <a href="mailto:support@astrx.dev">support@astrx.dev</a>. Bug
        reports and feature requests:
        <a
          href="https://github.com/dev-asterix/NexQL/issues"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issues</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="legal-footer-note">
      See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. · <a href="/">Back to NexQL</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</LegalLayout>
